📁 File Systems in the Cloud – AWS SimuLearn
Assignment: Pet modeling agency – share files across branch offices without managing physical storage.

🎯 What I Learned
Amazon EFS is a serverless, scalable file system for Linux EC2 instances – multiple instances can mount it at once.

EFS vs other storage: EBS is single-instance block storage, S3 is object storage (API access), but EFS is a shared file system (NFS protocol).

Real-world use case: A company with multiple branch offices can use EFS to share files centrally without buying or maintaining physical storage hardware.

Hands-on skills: Created an EFS file system, configured mount targets in VPC subnets, mounted EFS on multiple EC2 instances, and tested cross-instance file sharing.

🛠️ AWS Services Used
Amazon EC2 (virtual servers)

Amazon EFS (shared file storage)

✅ Key Takeaway
Cloud file systems remove infrastructure management – just create, mount, and share.
